    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40113" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιμᾰνής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>mad after</i>, a thing, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἐ. εἰς τὰς γυναῖκας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Paus.
					1.6.8
				</span></i>
			; so 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός τινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ach.Tat.
					8.1
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-νῶς, ἔχειν πρός τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ath.
					7.276e
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>. abs.,
				<i>raving, mad</i>, parody of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐπιφανής</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				26.1a
			</span></i>.<i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νόσημα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Dio</u>
					47
				</span></i>
			: 
				Comp.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-εστέρα, αἰσχρουογία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Pseudol.</u>
					21
				</span></i>
			.</div>
